              "title": "BITSAT 2024 (Memory Based Paper 1)"
            }
          ],
          "question": {
            "text": "$\\mathrm{A}(3,2,0), \\mathrm{B}(5,3,2), \\mathrm{C}(-9,6,-3)$ are three points forming a triangle. AD , the bisector of angle BAC meets BC in D. Find the co-ordinates of D.",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "pi1ao",
              "text": "$\\frac{19}{8}, \\frac{57}{15}, \\frac{57}{15}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "mi8fZ",
              "text": "$\\frac{19}{8}, \\frac{57}{16}, \\frac{17}{16}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "sY0LR",
              "text": "$(2,3,0)$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "12QZg",
              "text": "$(4,5,6)$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Since $A D$ is the bisector of $\\angle B A C$.\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{BD}}{\\mathrm{DC}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{AB}}{\\mathrm{AC}}$    ....(i)\nNow,\n$\\mathrm{AB}=\\sqrt{(5-3)^2+(3-2)^2+(2-0)^2}$\n$=\\sqrt{4+1+4}=\\sqrt{9}=3$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/CSbNXtILB1pcB-LkopQmKyTmNxU6GkvBypJfLzHuKOg.original.fullsize.png\"/>\n$A C=\\sqrt{(-9-3)^2+(6-2)^2+(-3-0)^2}$\n$=\\sqrt{144+16+9}=13$\n$\\therefore \\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{BD}}{\\mathrm{DC}}=\\frac{3}{13}$\nHence, D divides BC in the ratio $3: 13$\nThe co-ordinates of D are\n$\\left(\\frac{3(-9)+13(5)}{3+13}, \\frac{3(6)+13(3)}{3+13}, \\frac{3(-3)+13(2)}{3+13}\\right)$\n$=\\left(\\frac{19}{8}, \\frac{57}{16}, \\frac{17}{16}\\right)$",
            "image": null
          },
