    {
      "index": 3,
      "topicId": "64c0e86e6f5bfc7ab78aee1a",
      "title": "Condition for 2nd degree equationto represent pair of straight lines",
      "totalQuestions": 2,
      "questions": [
        {
          "_id": "64c0e8196f5bfc7ab78aea94",
          "previousYearPapers": [
            {
              "_id": "61a8bf0fc821b6514e527d7e",
              "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
              "heldOn": "2020-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
              "isVisible": true,
              "shortName": "2020",
              "title": "BITSAT 2020"
            }
          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "$Statement- 1$: If the general equation $x^{2}+y^{2}+2 x y+2 g x+2 f y+4=0$ represents a pair of real lines then $|\\mathrm{g}| \\geq 2$. \r\n\r\n$Statement- 2$: The equation $a x^{2}+2 h x y+b y^{2}+2 g x+2 f y+c=0$ represents pair\r\n\r\nof real lines if $a b c+2 f g h-a f^{2}-b g^{2}-c h^{2}=0$",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "KVhyg",
              "text": "Statement -1 is false, Statement- 2 is true",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "CUPsv",
              "text": "Statement -1 is true, Statement- 2 is true; Statement -2 is a correct explanation for Statement-1",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "vWYOq",
              "text": "Statement -1 is true, Statement- 2 is true; Statement -2 is not a correct explanation for Statement-1",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "VfCkI",
              "text": "Statement -1 is true, Statement- 2 is false",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "The equation represents a pair of lines if $1 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 4+2 \\cdot \\mathrm{f} \\cdot \\mathrm{g} \\cdot 1-1 \\cdot \\mathrm{f}^{2}-1 \\cdot \\mathrm{g}^{2}-4 \\cdot 1^{2}=0$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow(f-g)^{2}=0 \\Rightarrow f=g$\r\n\r\nThe equation becomes $(x+y)^{2}+2 g(x+y)+4=0$ Which represents pair of parallel lines, which are real provided $(2 \\mathrm{~g})^{2}-4 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 1 \\geq 0 \\Rightarrow|\\mathrm{g}| \\geq 2$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
          "questionStructure": [
            "default"
          ],
          "previousYear": {
