        {
          "_id": "64c0e7e36f5bfc7ab78ae8b7",
          "previousYearPapers": [
            {
              "_id": "61a8bf0fc821b6514e527d7a",
              "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
              "heldOn": "2016-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
              "isVisible": true,
              "shortName": "2016",
              "title": "BITSAT 2016"
            }
          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 1,
          "question": {
            "text": "The equation $x^{2}-2 \\sqrt{3} x y+3 y^{2}-3 x+3 \\sqrt{3} y-4=0 \\quad$ represents",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "jRDil",
              "text": "a pair of intersecting lines",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "vJrIh",
              "text": "a pair of parallel lines with distance between\r\n\r\nthem $\\frac{5}{2}$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "RzYel",
              "text": "a pair of parallel lines with distance between them $5 \\sqrt{2}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "OkRWq",
              "text": "a conic section, which is not a pair of straight lines",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "We have $a=1, h=-\\sqrt{3}, b=3, g=-\\frac{3}{2}$, $\\mathrm{f}=\\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2}, \\mathrm{c}=-4$\r\n\r\nThus $a b c+2 f g h-a f^{2}-b g^{2}-c h^{2}=0$\r\n\r\nHence the equation represents a pair of straight lines.\r\n\r\nAgain $\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{\\mathrm{h}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{\\mathrm{b}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{g}}{\\mathrm{f}}=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore$ the lines are parallel. The distance between them\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n=2 \\sqrt{\\frac{g^{2}-a c}{a(a+b)}}=2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{9}{4}+4}{1(1+3)}}=\\frac{5}{2}\r\n\r\n$$",
            "image": null
          },
